    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_88e981cc8f7cdc79ba9f77537d2794bfb28bb33de50855ed5a1f67d3c2f6bd42",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source supports a network of representation changes rather than one unconditional identity: integration by parts and parameter differentiation link weighted phase and log-modulus formulas while transporting explicit zero corrections; testing the zero-counting measure links weighted phase to sums over zero ordinates; and integrating the phase before applying a Littlewood relation links it to a horizontal log-modulus field. These bridges support the source's conditional identification of the Volchkov and Balazard-Saias-Yor criteria as differently written versions of a common zero-sensitive criterion. Pole cancellation supplies a related regularization-and-boundary-change example, but is not shown to be a step in that named-criterion chain.",
