    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fe7000ded67cc74e1e8035f1f616b4700bd372d25feeaf309f3e206055311a70",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source's criterion-construction recipe is constrained by the tractability of both the chosen contour kernel and every intermediate representation it creates. A kernel must support vanishing remote edges and computable contour contributions, while its off-line-zero correction must remain usable as an RH diagnostic; the two-scale example shows that a formally available integration-by-parts transfer can fail this test by replacing a rational weight with an analytically unmanageable logarithmic one.",
